import json,pathlib
r='frontier-40-geometry-braids-rep-27';p=pathlib.Path('research')/f'{r}-batch-25.pages.json';a=json.loads(p.read_text());src={'title':'The Stacks Project, Resolution of Surfaces, 54.7.7–8 and 54.8.8: dualizing module and relative duality support','url':'https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/download/resolve.pdf'}
def row(id,title,deps,statement,strategy,level=0):return dict(id=id,kind='lemma',title=title,deps=deps,statement=statement,strategy=strategy,design_row='AG-BIR-1',local_addition=True,provenance={'statement':'literature-derived','proof':'ai-altered'},sources={'references':[src]},dependency_level=level)
h1=row('lem-cm-local-codimension-and-regular-quotient-ext-concentration','CM local codimension and Ext concentration over a regular local ring',['def-axiom-of-choice','def-dependent-choice','lem-depth-localisation-inequality','cor-depth-of-a-finite-local-module-at-most-its-dimension','lem-associated-primes-of-cohen-macaulay-module-have-full-dimension','lem-regular-element-exists-by-prime-avoidance','cor-regular-quotient-cohen-macaulay-equivalence','thm-auslander-buchsbaum-formula','thm-regular-local-rings-are-domains-and-cohen-macaulay','lem-finite-closed-immersion-derived-coinduction-adjunction','lem-regular-quotient-dualizing-complex-and-biduality'],r'''Assume AC and DC. For a Noetherian CM local ring $R$ of dimension $D$ and every prime $\mathfrak p$, $D=\dim R_{\mathfrak p}+\dim R/\mathfrak p$. If $R$ is regular and $B=R/I\ne0$ is CM of dimension $e$, put $c=D-e$. Then $\operatorname{Ext}_R^q(B,R)=0$ for $q\ne c$. The canonical module $E=\operatorname{Ext}_R^c(B,R)$ is nonzero CM over $B$ and has full support. These conclusions localize.''',r'''The depth-localization inequality gives $D\le\operatorname{depth}R_{\mathfrak p}+\dim R/\mathfrak p\le\dim R_{\mathfrak p}+\dim R/\mathfrak p$. Concatenating chains below and above $\mathfrak p$ gives the reverse inequality, proving the dimension formula without a separate catenarity import. For regular $R$, Auslander–Buchsbaum gives $\operatorname{pd}_RB=D-e=c$, so Ext vanishes above $c$. The dimension formula gives height $I=c$. Inductively choose $f_1,\ldots,f_c\in I$ regular: after $j<c$ choices the quotient $Q=R/(f_1,\ldots,f_j)$ is CM of dimension $D-j$; every associated prime of $Q$ has quotient dimension $D-j$, hence height $j$ in $R$. None contains $I$, so prime avoidance gives the next regular element. The regular-quotient CM supplier drops dimension by one and preserves CM. For a regular element $f$ annihilating $B$, its two-term resolution and coinduction give $\operatorname{Ext}_Q^q(B,Q)=\operatorname{Ext}_{Q/fQ}^{q-1}(B,Q/fQ)$. Repeat through the regular tuple to get zero Ext below $c$. Dualize a finite free $R$-resolution of $B$ of length $c$; concentration makes its dual an exact resolution ending in $E$, so $\operatorname{pd}_RE\le c$. It is nonzero by canonical ambient biduality, and support lies in $V(I)$, hence dimension at most $e$. Auslander–Buchsbaum and the depth bound give $e\le\operatorname{depth}_RE\le\dim E\le e$, so it is CM. At any localization of $B$, a zero canonical module would make its dualizing complex zero and contradict homothety for the nonzero local ring, so support is full. The same finite resolutions and coinduction localize, giving the local conclusions. This generalizes the published field-polynomial Ext-concentration supplier by proving the missing codimension formula from an actual general CM supplier.''')
h2=row('lem-normal-projective-surface-dualizing-module-over-regular-local-base','Dualizing modules and trace pairing for normal projective surface modifications',['def-axiom-of-choice','def-dependent-choice','def-normal-surface-modification-and-normalized-point-blowup',h1['id'],'lem-projective-regular-local-base-coherent-duality-by-embedding','lem-finite-regular-base-algebra-dualizing-biduality','lem-finite-closed-immersion-derived-coinduction-adjunction','lem-normal-domain-implies-s-two','cor-every-system-of-parameters-is-regular-in-a-cohen-macaulay-module','thm-auslander-buchsbaum-formula','thm-quotient-and-lifting-regularity-across-a-regular-element','thm-localisation-and-polynomial-extension-of-regular-rings'],r'''Assume AC and DC. Let $R$ be a regular Noetherian local ring of dimension two, let $A$ be a finite normal local $R$-domain of dimension two, with $R\hookrightarrow A$ local, and let $X$ be a normal integral scheme of dimension two projective over $R$, with a proper birational map $f:X\to\operatorname{Spec}A$. Put $\omega_A=\operatorname{Hom}_R(A,R)$. The regular-base projective dualizing complex is canonically $D_X=\omega_X[2]$ with $\omega_X$ a coherent CM torsion-free module of generic rank one, and $D_A=\omega_A[2]$. Evaluation gives $R\Gamma(X,\omega_X)\cong R\operatorname{Hom}_A(R\Gamma(X,\mathcal O_X),\omega_A)$. Its trace to $\omega_A$ is the dual of $A\to R\Gamma(X,\mathcal O_X)$; these are pairings of complexes with their natural $A$-actions.''',r'''Normality's S2 condition makes all local rings of $A$ and $X$ CM, since their dimensions are at most two. A regular parameter pair of $R$ generates an ideal primary to the maximal ideal of the finite local algebra $A$, so is a system of parameters there and is $A$-regular. Thus $\operatorname{depth}_R A=2$ and Auslander–Buchsbaum makes $A$ finite free over $R$. Hence the finite-base dualizing complex is $\operatorname{Hom}_R(A,R)[2]$. Fix a projective embedding $X\hookrightarrow\mathbb P_R^N$. At a closed point, properness puts the image in the closed fibre and its residue field is finite over that of $R$. The ambient polynomial local ring has dimension $N+2$: its parameter pair from $R$ is regular and quotienting gives the $N$-dimensional regular polynomial local ring over the residue field. Its prime ideal defining the integral affine chart of $X$ has height $N$: it avoids nonzero $R$-elements and localization to $\operatorname{Frac}R$ gives a polynomial ring in $N$ variables modulo a prime with finite residue field extension (the generic field of $X$ is finite over $\operatorname{Frac}R$). Chains below that prime all avoid the same multiplicative set, so their heights are unchanged. The preceding CM dimension formula gives local dimension two on $X$, and Ext concentration gives $D_X$ only in degree $-2$ at this closed point. Every point of the proper Noetherian scheme specializes to a closed point, so coherent cohomology sheaves vanish globally outside that degree. The same Ext argument makes $\omega_X$ CM with full support. The full-dimension associated-prime property on its local CM stalks makes it torsion-free on the normal integral surface. At the generic point homothety identifies its endomorphisms with the function field, so its finite-dimensional generic vector space has rank one. The projective regular-base complex duality applied to $K=\mathcal O_X$, followed by finite-ring coinduction and cancellation of the common shift two, gives the displayed quasi-isomorphism. All arrows are evaluation/coinduction pairings, so the induced trace is exactly dual to the unit on structure-sheaf cohomology and is $A$-linear. No smoothness, perfect ground field, or general proper f-shriek theorem was imported.''',3)
for h in [h1,h2]:
 idx=next(i for i,x in enumerate(a[0]['items']) if x['id']=='thm-resolution-of-normal-surface-singularities');a[0]['items'].insert(idx,h)
